## Core concepts (three layers, all FSRS-backed)

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    subgraph itemLayer [Item confidence - FSRS]
        RI["ReviewItem (stability, difficulty, due, ...)"]
        R["R = ForgettingCurve(now)"]
        RI --> R
    end

    subgraph levelLayer [Level progress - fixed curriculum + FSRS]
        LC["LevelCurriculum: A0=100 words, ..."]
        VLC["mastered_count / curriculum_size"]
        GLC["grammar_gate + weak topic set"]
        R --> VLC
        R --> GLC
        LC --> VLC
    end

    subgraph probLayer [New-item probability - dynamic]
        PNEW["P(new) = headroom × confidence_gate"]
        VLC --> PNEW
        R --> PNEW
    end

    subgraph sessionLayer [Session assembly]
        QP[QuizPlanner]
        PNEW --> QP
        GLC --> QP
        R --> QP
    end
```

1. **Item confidence** — `R(item)` from FSRS card. Drives scheduling, **task modality**, and sentence complexity sampling.
2. **Level metrics** — Fixed curriculum sizes per CEFR level (e.g. 100 A0 words = A1-ready). Progress = count of words/topics above FSRS confidence threshold. Drives level promotion.
3. **New-item probability** — Dynamic per session, derived from avg FSRS confidence + curriculum headroom. Low confidence → strengthen before introducing new items (vocab and grammar).
4. **Sentence complexity** — Probabilistic pick of example sentence level, weighted by level progress.

