```
VOCAB_CURRICULUM(L)    = top N words by frequency_rank at level L
GRAMMAR_CURRICULUM(L)  = grammar_blocks at level L with exemplar+exercise, by sort_order
```

### Word states (FSRS-derived)

```
R(w) = 0                         if no review_item
R(w) = FSRS.ForgettingCurve(now) otherwise

mastered(w) = R(w) >= MASTERED_THRESHOLD   // 0.90 — aligns with FSRS desired retention
touched(w)  = review_item exists
new(w)      = not touched(w)
```

### Level progress (what user sees)

```
mastered_count(L) = count(w in CURRICULUM(L) where mastered(w))
level_progress(L) = mastered_count(L) / LevelCurriculum.target_word_count(L)
```

Example: 73 of 100 A0 words with R ≥ 0.90 → **A0 progress = 73%**.

### Level promotion rules (research-informed)

```
# Soft unlock — start seeing L+1 words in quiz
level_progress(L) >= 0.70          // ~70% of curriculum stable; i+1 input range

# Hard unlock — update current_level_id
level_progress(vocab, L) >= 0.70
AND grammar_exposure(L)           # all grammar topics seen once
AND grammar_avg_R(L) >= 0.35      # lower than vocab — ongoing revision expected

# Full level complete (display badge)
level_progress(L) >= 1.0           // all curriculum words at R >= 0.90
```

Sprinkling L+1 before 100% completion is supported by i+1 research (Nation, Krashen) — waiting for 100% causes boredom; 70% is a reasonable blend start.

